│ patch_description        │ Replace the random point placement with an actual optimizer. The objective is             │
│                          │ scale/translation/rotation invariant, so we can fix the diameter (max pairwise distance)  │
│                          │ to 1 and maximize the minimum pairwise distance. Equivalently minimize a smooth           │
│                          │ surrogate: -log(sum over pairs of exp(-alpha*d_ij^2))-ish, but simpler and robust: use a  │
│                          │ soft-min via -1/k * log(sum exp(-k*d_ij)) over pairs with a penalty pushing dmax to 1. We │
│                          │ run scipy's L-BFGS-B from several fixed-seed random starts plus structured starts         │
│                          │ (icosahedron vertices + centers, cuboctahedron-based), pick the best configuration by the │
│                          │ true (dmin/dmax)^2 metric, and return the points. This should get close to the reference  │
│                          │ squared ratio 1/4.1658 (~0.2399), giving a combined score near 1.                         │
