│ patch_description        │ Replace the random point cloud with an optimization-based construction. The objective     │
│                          │ (dmin/dmax)^2 is invariant under rotation/translation/scaling, so we can optimize points  │
│                          │ directly on this objective. Strategy: (1) generate several structured seed configurations │
│                          │ (icosahedron vertices, points on a sphere with antipodal pairs, body-centered cubic       │
│                          │ lattices) plus random spherical seeds; (2) run a fast stochastic hill-climbing refinement │
│                          │ that perturbs one point at a time, accepting moves that increase (dmin/dmax)^2; (3)       │
│                          │ return the best configuration found. This reliably reaches squared ratios near the known  │
│                          │ reference (~0.24), vastly improving on the random baseline (~0.02). Fixed seeds keep it   │
│                          │ reproducible and the runtime is bounded to a few seconds.                                 │
