│                          │ and directly maximize dmin/dmax using a smooth soft-min/soft-max surrogate minimized by   │
│                          │ L-BFGS-B over multiple fixed-seed restarts (including structured starts like the          │
│                          │ icosahedron). After optimization, we shift/scale so the configuration is centered and     │
│                          │ normalized (objective is invariant to this). The smooth surrogate (log-sum-exponential of │
│                          │ distances) is differentiable, letting BFGS make progress on this non-smooth objective;    │
│                          │ the best restart by the true ratio is kept. This should raise the ratio from ~0 (random   │
│                          │ points often have near-coincident min distances) to near the reference ~0.49.             │
