│ patch_name               │ sphere_repulsion_optimizer                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the random point placement with a proper continuous optimizer: initialize 14      │
│                          │ points on a unit sphere (with symmetry to avoid degenerate starts), then run projected    │
│                          │ gradient ascent maximizing a soft-minimum of the pairwise distances, rescaling each       │
│                          │ iteration so dmax = 1. Since the objective dmin/dmax is scale invariant, fixing dmax = 1  │
│                          │ and maximizing the (soft) minimum distance directly optimizes the ratio. A softmin        │
│                          │ (log-sum-exp) gives smooth gradients everywhere, and a final fine-tuning pass with a      │
│                          │ small temperature sharpens the true minimum. This is a standard relaxation approach for   │
│                          │ Tammes/packing problems and should reach a squared ratio near the known reference         │
│                          │ (~1/4.17).                                                                                │
