│ patch_description        │ Instead of random points (score 0.02), I use a smooth surrogate optimization: the hard    │
│                          │ ratio dmin/dmax is replaced by a differentiable soft-min/soft-max over pairwise distances │
│                          │ (log-sum-exp with temperature), optimized by L-BFGS-B gradient ascent from many seeded    │
│                          │ restarts (including structured starts from the icosahedron plus two poles, and cube       │
│                          │ vertices + centers, which are known-good packings). As the temperature anneals, the       │
│                          │ smooth ratio converges to the true ratio. We keep the best true (dmin/dmax)^2 found       │
│                          │ across all restarts. This directly targets the evaluator's metric and typically reaches   │
│                          │ squared ratios near the known reference (~1/4.166 ≈ 0.24) for 14 points in 3D, orders of  │
│                          │ magnitude above the current score.                                                        │
