│ patch_name               │ annealed_slsqp_polish                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current soft-min/soft-max objective is scale-coupled and its Nelder-Mead polish is    │
│                          │ inefficient. I replace it with: (1) a scale-normalized soft-min objective with            │
│                          │ k-annealing (k = 8 → 120) under L-BFGS-B, which is smoother early and sharp later; (2)    │
│                          │ many structured starts (icosahedron+poles, Fibonacci sphere, jittered versions, random    │
│                          │ sphere points); (3) an exact polish via SLSQP that directly maximizes the true nonsmooth  │
│                          │ problem: maximize t subject to t² ≤ ||pi−pj||² ≤ 1 for all pairs, with analytic           │
│                          │ Jacobians, plus a few perturbed restarts of the polish. This targets a true dmin/dmax     │
│                          │ beyond the reference 0.4897 (squared 0.24).                                               │
