│                          │ noticeably smooths the true ratio). I add (1) a deeper annealing stage (T=0.02, 0.01),    │
│                          │ and (2) a final L-BFGS-B polish directly on the exact objective f = (dmin/dmax)^2, using  │
│                          │ the correct analytic gradient via the argmin/argmax pair (chain rule through the two      │
│                          │ active distances). This gradient-following polish on the true (nonsmooth but piecewise)   │
│                          │ objective can squeeze the ratio past the soft surrogate's plateau, potentially exceeding  │
│                          │ the reference score of 1. Runtime stays small since it only runs once per start.          │
