│ patch_description        │ Diversify initialization away from the 0.24 basin with several structured candidates      │
│                          │ (icosahedron + poles at varied heights and axes, Fibonacci-sphere spiral, cuboctahedron + │
│                          │ poles, antiprism-like, and random sphere starts). For each start, run SLSQP maximizing    │
│                          │ the minimum squared distance t subject to all squared pairwise distances ≥ t and ≤ 1      │
│                          │ (fixing the diameter to 1, which makes the min/max ratio directly = sqrt(t)). Track the   │
│                          │ best true ratio across all starts and return the normalized winner. This constrained      │
│                          │ formulation directly optimizes the exact objective instead of a softmin surrogate, and    │
│                          │ the varied structured starts escape the icosahedron+poles basin.                          │
