│ patch_name               │ analytic_gradient_ascent_slsqp_polish                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the slow numerical-gradient L-BFGS-B and ineffective Nelder-Mead stages with (a)  │
│                          │ a fast annealed analytic-gradient ascent on a soft-minimum of the pairwise distances      │
│                          │ (with points kept centered and scaled so dmax=1 after every step, which handles scale     │
│                          │ invariance exactly), and (b) the exact SLSQP polish (maximize t subject to t^2 <=         │
│                          │ ||pi-pj||^2 <= 1) from the 1.00-scoring program, plus jitter restarts of the polish. This │
│                          │ is ~20x faster per optimization run than L-BFGS-B with numerical gradients, freeing       │
│                          │ budget for many more structured/random starts, while the SLSQP stage polishes to the best │
│                          │ known configuration.                                                                      │
