│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ratio_grad_slsqp_polish                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The previous program wasted a broken gradient and relied on a scale-free softmin          │
│                          │ surrogate whose optimum drifts from the true ratio. The rewrite:                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Optimizes the actual smooth ratio f = −smin/smax (softmin/softmax over the 91 pairwise │
│                          │ distances) with a correct, vectorized analytic gradient: dsmin/dp_a = Σ_b (w_ab/W)·u_ab,  │
│                          │ dsmax/dp_a = Σ_b (w′_ab/W′)·u_ab, df/dp_a = −(dsmin·smax − smin·dsmax)/smax². Softmax     │
│                          │ weights are computed with max-subtraction for numerical stability, so sharp k values (up  │
│                          │ to 200) are usable without overflow.                                                      │
│                          │ 2. Anneals k (15 → 60 → 200) inside L-BFGS-B, driving the surrogate toward the true       │
│                          │ min/max ratio in the limit.                                                               │
│                          │ 3. Finishes with an exact SLSQP polish: maximize t subject to t² ≤ ‖pi−pj‖² ≤ 1 for all   │
│                          │ pairs (vectorized Jacobian), which is a direct nonlinear program for the true objective   │
│                          │ after normalizing dmax = 1.                                                               │
│                          │ 4. Uses many structured starts (icosahedron+poles, Fibonacci sphere, jittered variants,   │
│                          │ random spherical and Gaussian clouds) with a fixed seed, and keeps the best true ratio    │
│                          │ across all runs, plus jittered re-polishes of the leader.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This removes the dead/incorrect gradient code, targets the true metric throughout, and    │
│                          │ should reliably reach or slightly beat the reference squared ratio 1/4.1658.              │
