│                          │ program's fast softmin gradient "spreading" preprocessor, which is used (a) to generate   │
│                          │ additional pre-conditioned random seeds before the Adam stage, and (b) as a cheap         │
│                          │ repulsion spreader. I then vectorize the SLSQP constraints (single array-valued           │
│                          │ constraint function with an analytic dense Jacobian built via fancy indexing instead of   │
│                          │ 182 separate Python closures), which makes each SLSQP call much faster, leaving budget    │
│                          │ for extra polish: alternating fine-tau Adam + SLSQP rounds plus noise-perturbation SLSQP  │
│                          │ restarts around the incumbent best. The final result is centered and normalized to        │
│                          │ diameter 1. The true objective (min(d²)/max(d²)) is what is tracked throughout, so any    │
│                          │ configuration that beats the reference squared ratio 1/4.1658 will push combined_score    │
│                          │ above 1. Fixed seeds and guards ensure reproducibility and a valid finite (14,3) return.  │
