                        Patch Metadata - Gen 40/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ force_balance_slsqp_14pts                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ A completely different algorithm: instead of soft-minimum annealing, I use a              │
│                          │ physics-style force-balance relaxation (each pair is connected by a nonlinear spring:     │
│                          │ pairs shorter than the current min-distance get repulsive forces, pairs near the diameter │
│                          │ get weak attractive forces) combined with projection back to dmax=1 after each step. This │
│                          │ "Thomson-like" relaxation with diameter pressure naturally flows toward equal-distance    │
│                          │ packings. Then a final exact constrained SLSQP polish (maximize t s.t. t² ≤ d²ij ≤ 1)     │
│                          │ locks the configuration to a true local optimum of the exact squared ratio. Structured    │
│                          │ seeds cover distinct geometric families (staggered heptagon rings, icosahedron+poles,     │
│                          │ cuboctahedron+poles, rhombic-dodecahedron-like, Fibonacci sphere), and a degenerate-basin │
│                          │ check reallocates effort. The approach avoids the softmax-ratio plateau because the force │
│                          │ model targets distance *equality* directly rather than a smoothed ratio objective.        │
