│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ slsqp_minmax_14                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of stochastic annealing, use constrained nonlinear optimization (SLSQP) to        │
│                          │ directly maximize the minimum pairwise distance: after normalizing so dmax = 1, we solve  │
│                          │ max t subject to ||pi-pj||² ≥ t² for all 91 pairs with t ≤ 1, providing analytic          │
│                          │ constraint Jacobians. This is a smooth, principled local solver that converges to true    │
│                          │ local optima of the spread problem rather than a random-walk basin. Applied from a        │
│                          │ diverse family of structured seeds (Fibonacci sphere, cuboctahedron+poles sweep,          │
│                          │ icosahedron+poles sweeps, staggered heptagon rings, fixed-seed random configs), it        │
│                          │ reliably reaches (and often exceeds) the reference configuration ratio of ~0.49, whereas  │
│                          │ annealing was stuck near 0.48.                                                            │
