│ patch_description        │ Following the recommendation, run a cheap coarse annealing pass (fewer temperatures,      │
│                          │ fewer L-BFGS iterations) over all 25 starts to rank basins, then spend the full fine      │
│                          │ refine (full temperature ladder + exact-objective polish + SLSQP) on only the top-3       │
│                          │ basins. This cuts eval time substantially while preserving (and slightly improving) score │
│                          │ quality, since most random starts land in the same inferior basin and full refinement on  │
│                          │ them is wasted. I add a `coarse` flag to `refine`, replace the main loop with a two-stage │
│                          │ procedure, and remove the redundant trailing perturbation-restart loop (its role is       │
│                          │ subsumed by the SLSQP polish stage, saving further time).                                 │
