│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ moment_homotopy_epigraph_tiers                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This design replaces the log-sum-exp softmin/softmax surrogate used by the previous       │
│                          │ programs with a fundamentally different smooth, scale-invariant objective: the "moment    │
│                          │ product" f_q = log(Σ s^q) + log(Σ s^{-q}) over squared pair distances s. As q → ∞,        │
│                          │ minimizing f_q drives dmax² down and dmin² up simultaneously (q-th moments of s and 1/s   │
│                          │ approximate the extremes), and it is exactly scale-invariant for every q, so it forms a   │
│                          │ natural homotopy: small q optimizes globally-smooth average-based geometry, large q       │
│                          │ sharpens toward the true min/max ratio. Gradients are computed stably in log-space via    │
│                          │ logsumexp-style softmax weights (no overflow for large q).                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The pipeline is organized as budget-tiered screening (inspired by the runtime-reduction   │
│                          │ recommendation): (1) a cheap screen anneals q ∈ {0.6, 2.5} with short L-BFGS-B runs over  │
│                          │ ~21 diverse structured seeds (staggered hexagonal double-rings with poles,                │
│                          │ icosahedron+poles, cube+face-pushes, antipodal 7-direction pairs, and repulsion-spread    │
│                          │ randoms via a Coulomb-like descent); (2) only the top 5 basins receive the deep anneal (q │
│                          │ ∈ {6, 20}) plus the exact nonsmooth (dmin/dmax)² gradient polish with decaying jitter     │
│                          │ restarts; (3) the top 2 candidates get a final epigraph SLSQP stage that directly         │
│                          │ maximizes t subject to t ≤ |x_i−x_j|² ≤ 1 (the exact mathematical program for the         │
│                          │ problem, with a vectorized 182-row constraint Jacobian), which can squeeze marginal gains │
│                          │ beyond what the kinked L-BFGS objective reaches. All stages compare on the exact true     │
│                          │ ratio, keep the best, and the result is normalized so dmax = 1.                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
